 r←SecretIniKeys
⍝ Parts of INI key names, in upper case, that mark a value as a credential: an INI entry whose key
⍝ contains any of them is shown as "***" in the start-up report (see `CollectStartParms`).
⍝ `[LOGGING]MaskIniKeys` in the INI file adds to them: see `EstablishSecrets`.
⍝ "KEY" on its own is not among them: it would hide entries such as `PrivateKeyFile`, which hold paths.
 r←'PASSWORD' 'PASSWD' 'SECRET' 'TOKEN' 'APIKEY' 'API_KEY' 'CREDENTIAL'
